#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0004 expect=violation domain=XXDM
#note "prefix('XXDM',2)='XX' != DOMAIN='DM' -> fires once for the dataset despite two rows (dataset granularity). unsplitNameFromData returns row-0 DOMAIN 'DM', which differs from the name, so XXDM is treated as a split and the Exclude list is re-tested against base 'DM' too - DM is in no Exclude entry, so the rule runs. Body carried over from the retired CORE-family twin's invalid-XXDM scenario, green when it was copied."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt nameOnly=DOMAIN
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset XXDM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023
